{"agent_id":"pp3g-5YO2-research-task-issue-133-find-a-background-completion","agent_seq":9,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T03:46:23.957858479Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"e17b7dd1-ee7c-4462-bf98-4dc7b28a11b5","comment_uuid":"3bd6e95b-0f35-4fa0-b049-a8ce969fcd59","author":"pp3g-5YO2-research-task-issue-133-find-a-background-completion","content":"VERDICT — Recommendation: add a small user-level systemd timer watcher for kickoff status files, not sentinel or an OpenCode plugin, as the cheapest mechanism that covers the actual blind spot. Evidence: (1) local crosslink sentinel is disabled here;  is one-shot and  is a persistent poller (default 10m), but its configured  source only discovers  labels. It dispatches/collects sentinel-owned rows, and its existing  sends completion POSTs (Slack or generic JSON) only from  for those rows; it does not watch arbitrary  files. (2) kickoff itself writes LAUNCHING/RUNNING and agents write terminal DONE/FAILED/CI_FAILED to ; this is the authoritative completion signal and is independent of which agent binary is used. (3) OpenCode's official plugin API does expose , , , and a documented notification example; community plugins , , and  provide desktop/bell/subagent notifications. They only observe OpenCode session events, however; they cannot see a Claude/tmux kickoff unless every dispatched agent is OpenCode, so they are not a complete solution. (4) freedesktop notifications are a standard asynchronous desktop channel; this host currently lacks , so libnotify is an explicit prerequisite. Implementation sketch: add  (stdlib only) that scans  every 15–30s, records  in , and emits once per terminal transition via ; optionally POST the same JSON to a configured webhook with curl for remote/headless operators. Add  (oneshot, , ExecStart=python3 tools/kickoff-notify.py) and  (, , ), then run  (or distro equivalent), , . Filter only DONE/FAILED/CI_FAILED and retain state so repeated scans are silent; include a cleanup/expiry policy for removed worktrees. This avoids changing kickoff or sentinel semantics, catches all kickoff agents, survives the operator switching windows, and remains inspectable with -- No entries --. Alternatives: enable sentinel + configure its existing webhook only if all dispatches are sentinel-owned; install an OpenCode notifier only as an optional secondary signal.","created_at":"2026-08-03T03:46:23.950948781Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:bXk3q5wQqFr+NjuZvakfJH0YrD4Qv3fzYaZY5FdaMpc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgKvuCNQQEvKFknLQBzfzPYsppWPbKl+Z24AbD5zhV2KsAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAAbfgg6Q0OXY5aD5FAcRbya7QRHuSEpgrZ11gfpsbNIDViL8JWFlfssI3vKyAHlLTsIpBDQAQhrpWSSliVBIUCA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:bXk3q5wQqFr+NjuZvakfJH0YrD4Qv3fzYaZY5FdaMpc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgKvuCNQQEvKFknLQBzfzPYsppWPbKl+Z24AbD5zhV2KsAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGDY3Kpvks7hi3rBcENXU9ZXxjdOkK98pf6x9NPIhVU2uxKFxq1+Pj4/MZmnxMSjZm6QM6tAWgtDbQ2ZtJYwlAY="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-5YO2-research-task-issue-133-find-a-background-completion","agent_seq":10,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T03:46:37.582135543Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"e17b7dd1-ee7c-4462-bf98-4dc7b28a11b5","comment_uuid":"81a2257f-2bd9-4ede-b5ef-2ee451863c08","author":"pp3g-5YO2-research-task-issue-133-find-a-background-completion","content":"VERDICT (corrected structured summary): RECOMMEND a user-level systemd timer plus a stdlib Python watcher for worktree kickoff status files. Why: crosslink sentinel is a maintenance dispatcher, not a general completion watcher. Local CLI confirms run is one-shot and watch is a persistent poller (default 10 minutes). Configured github_labels only discovers agent-todo labels. Sentinel has outbound Slack or generic JSON completion webhooks, but collect_completed calls them only for sentinel-owned dispatch database rows. It does not watch arbitrary kickoff worktrees. Kickoff writes LAUNCHING and RUNNING, then terminal DONE, FAILED, or CI_FAILED in each worktree status file; this is the authoritative signal and covers any agent binary. OpenCode plugins officially receive session.idle, session.error, tool.execute.after, and can invoke OS notifications. Community packages include @mohak34/opencode-notifier, opencode-notificator, and opencode-notify. They observe OpenCode sessions only, so they do not close this gap when kickoff runs Claude or another tmux agent. Implementation sketch: add tools/kickoff-notify.py, using only Python standard library, scanning REPO/.worktrees/*/.kickoff-status every 15 to 30 seconds; persist path plus status plus mtime in a state file; notify once for DONE, FAILED, and CI_FAILED transitions using notify-send, with optional curl POST to a configured webhook for headless or remote operation. Add user units ases-kickoff-notify.service (oneshot, WorkingDirectory=REPO, ExecStart=python3 REPO/tools/kickoff-notify.py) and ases-kickoff-notify.timer (OnBootSec=15s, OnUnitActiveSec=15s, Persistent=true). Install libnotify-bin or the distro equivalent, then run systemctl --user daemon-reload and systemctl --user enable --now ases-kickoff-notify.timer. Retain state and expire entries for deleted worktrees; inspect with journalctl --user -u ases-kickoff-notify. This is independent of sentinel and catches all kickoff agents. Enable sentinel notifications only as a secondary option when every dispatch is sentinel-owned; install an OpenCode notifier only as a secondary signal.","created_at":"2026-08-03T03:46:37.575991078Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:bXk3q5wQqFr+NjuZvakfJH0YrD4Qv3fzYaZY5FdaMpc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgKvuCNQQEvKFknLQBzfzPYsppWPbKl+Z24AbD5zhV2KsAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAukhSeZgcr4nnaO+BI6HzvlfMVf9C1jRBxLPpcwh1/QzG/SgmHznrHXKj+DKo9LqHtGP2y+3qweIk8yV2YOp3Cg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:bXk3q5wQqFr+NjuZvakfJH0YrD4Qv3fzYaZY5FdaMpc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgKvuCNQQEvKFknLQBzfzPYsppWPbKl+Z24AbD5zhV2KsAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCgbOVJiOC5IB6IeG1emv3MR64SfReYXr3ajl+PSVvmu2izY+BdpCxXI5jmvYb9QkDbTMc3nYOjCtWpMbwmj+wM="}
